text.paragraph:
Dose adjustments may be needed when ranolazine extended-release tablets are taken in combination with certain other drugs [see Drug Interactions (7.1)
                           ]. Limit the maximum dose of ranolazine extended-release tablets to 500 mg twice daily in patients on moderate CYP3A inhibitors such as diltiazem, verapamil, and erythromycin. Use of ranolazine extended-release tablets with strong CYP3A inhibitors is contraindicated [see Contraindications (4), Drug Interactions (7.1)
                           ]. Use of P-gp inhibitors, such as cyclosporine, may increase exposure to ranolazine extended-release tablets. Titrate ranolazine extended-release tablets based on clinical response [see Drug Interactions (7.1)
                           ].
